  "validation_notes": {
    "match_threshold_rationale": "0.85 chosen for cosine similarity over embedding space. Below this, lexical drift becomes too large (e.g., 'authoritative' vs 'commanding' should match; 'authoritative' vs 'serious' should not).",
    "ambiguity_window_rationale": "0.05 — if two canonical keys both score above threshold and within 0.05 of each other, treat as ambiguous and flag for human review rather than auto-mapping.",
    "fallback_threshold_rationale": "difflib.SequenceMatcher with 0.7 ratio. Stricter than the semantic threshold because lexical similarity is a weaker signal than embedding similarity.",
    "domain_specific_keys": "Several keys (investor_type, holding_period, engagement_with_ir_communications, proxy_vote_participation_pct, earnings_call_attendance) are tuned to the AS Radiant investor-calibration use case visible in fixture data. Generalize the vocabulary per-engagement when calibrating non-investor audiences."
  }
